Backend – FedEx Surround Data Flow
FedEx Tracking Event
→ SurroundTrackingEventController.handleTrackingEvent()
→ Validate FDX_SIGNATURE and FDX_SUBSCRIPTION_ID headers
→ Generate expected signature using FedexTrackingEventHashCalculator.encode(requestBody)
→ Compare FedEx signature with expected signature
→ If valid, call publish(requestBody)
→ Parse payload using ObjectMapper
→ Create SurroundDataDTO and TrackingWebhookDTO
→ Call TrackingWebhookService.webhookPublisher()
→ TrackingWebhookServiceImpl.publish()
→ Serialize TrackingWebhookDTO using ObjectMapper
→ MessagingPublisher.publish()
→ Publish message to GCP topic: ADVSHIP_TRACKING_FEDEX_SURROUND
→ Downstream services consume and process the tracking event.
Key Points
The Surround Edge Service acts as the entry point for FedEx tracking events.
Requests are validated for required FedEx headers and signature before publishing.
The incoming FedEx payload is transformed into the application's TrackingWebhookDTO.
The validated event is published to GCP Messaging for downstream processing.
Unknown fields in the FedEx payload are ignored using FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES = false, allowing the service to handle additional fields from FedEx without failing.